<BaseLayout title="About" description="CAPIBARA is an international, student-led initiative building the next generation of space observatories.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About the CAPIBARA Collaboration</h1>

    <p>
      <strong>We are an international, student-led initiative building the next generation of space observatories.</strong>
      Our mission is to advance high-energy astrophysics while creating a vertically integrated training platform
      for the next generation of scientists and engineers. Through hands-on development of real space hardware and
      open collaboration, we are proving that students can contribute meaningfully to cutting-edge scientific discovery.
    </p>

    <p>
      The collaboration operates two parallel programs: <strong>CAPIBARA-CRD</strong>, developing a cosmic ray detector
      for near-Earth space weather monitoring to fly on the OBA FARADAY satellite, and <strong>CAPIBARA-COSMOS</strong>,
      our flagship effort to build a scalable gamma-ray/X-ray satellite constellation. COSMOS follows a deliberate growth
      path — starting with a single CubeSat pathfinder, advancing to a dual-satellite demonstrator for triangulation, and
      culminating in an operational network of four observatories by 2035.
    </p>

    <p>
      We are more than a project; we are building a lasting model for student-led research. Every design document,
      simulation, and hardware prototype is developed collaboratively across universities worldwide, creating both
      scientific instruments and the skilled workforce to operate them. <strong>No experience required — only passion
      and willingness to learn.</strong>
    </p>

    <h2>Why join us?</h2>
    <p>
      Beyond hardware and science, CAPIBARA is about building a community of the new generation of space experts.
      We're creating a collaboration where students don't just learn about space — they actually engage with it.
    </p>

    <h3>For students</h3>
    <p>
      Work on real flight hardware and software, with simulations and operations. CAPIBARA is not only engineering,
      but also science, outreach and communication. <a href="/join/">Apply here</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>For advisors</h3>
    <p>
      Mentor the next generation. Join the COSMOS advisory board or contact the CRD team.
      <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>For institutions</h3>
    <p>
      Partner with us, provide lab space, expertise or funding, or host a student team.
      <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
